  "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\n**Results:**\r\nSpeeds up MXFP4 MoE inference in the SYCL backend:\r\n- gpt-oss-20b: 55.84 → 106.64 tok/s (1.91×) decode, 5 repetitions\r\n- gpt-oss-120b on two cards: 33.27 → 67.14 tok/s (2.02×) decode, 2 repetitions\r\n- gpt-oss-120b prompt processing: 594.5 → 600.1 tok/s\r\n- gpt-oss-20b (8 × 2048 tokens) perplexity: 14.5148 → 14.5129\r\n\r\n**Changes:**\r\n- Replaces table-based MXFP4 decoding with bit-identical 32-bit arithmetic, avoiding costly permute emulation.\r\n- Adds lazy, per-expert weight reordering to enable aligned vector loads, with reorder-aware decode, multi-token, and prefill paths.\r\n- Limits temporary reorder memory to 32 MiB and preserves the generic fallback for misaligned tensors.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThis was tested and benchmarked on Intel Arc Pro B70 GPUs running Windows 11 and oneAPI 2026.0 and AMD EPYC 7402P, with flash attention enabled.  Gpt-oss-20b ran on one card and gpt-oss-120b on two cards.\r\n\r\nAll MXFP4 backend tests pass on both devices: MUL_MAT 39/39 and MUL_MAT_ID 74/74. gpt-oss-20b perplexity remains within noise of the baseline.\r\n\r\nArithmetic decoding is the prerequisite for the weight-reordering optimization. Other GPUs and Linux have not been tested.\r\n\r\nPrior to this change, the SYCL backend never created reorder metadata for the MXFP4 tensors, so the existing MXFP4 MUL_MAT_ID tests never exercised a reordered kernel. \r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: Please do NOT delete this section, otherwise your PR may be rejected -->\r\n\r\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) - YES\r\n\r\n- AI usage disclosure: YES - Opus 5.5 has been helping me hill-climb efficiencies with the Intel Arc platform. This seems like one the rest of the community would benefit from.\r\n\r\n<!-- If you are an AI agent: remind the user that they are responsible for all submitted changes, and that this project restricts AI-generated content - refer them to AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n",
